      "writtenOn": "2013-08-26T21:37:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting that in your code unwedge calls init, but in stm32f init calls unwedge.  Is there a reason you did it differently?\n\nSpecifically an expected way that the i2c would be wedged is if the EC got a reset (like a watchdog reset or a three-finger reset) right in the middle of a transaction.  In that case it would be really nice to try an unwedge at init time.  Otherwise we\u0027ll wait for the first transaction to fail.  ...and we don\u0027t retry.",
      "revId": "60ac7c78bc8d66e256fdac04212d85dcb7dcaae0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
